@startuml seq_008_authorization_check
!include common/seq_styles.puml

title SEQ-008 Authorization Check\nCapability-Based Access Control with SoD

actor "User" as user
participant "selma_interface\n(CLI/WebApp/DesktopApp/MobileApp)" as SI #EBCB8B
participant "application_service\n(FastAPI/Pydantic)" as AS #88C0D0
participant "findings_audit_adapter\n(Python/SHA-256/Append-Only)" as FAA #D08770
database "event_store\n(Append-Only Log)" as ES #4C566A

autonumber

user -> SI: request with credentials
activate SI

SI -> AS: REST request (with auth token)
activate AS

group Authentication
    AS -> AS: authenticate (extract actor identity)
    note right of AS
        Verify token signature.
        Extract actor_id and roles.
    end note
end

group Capability Check
    AS -> AS: load actor capabilities
    AS -> AS: check required capability

    alt Capability Denied
        AS -> FAA: append CapabilityDenied event
        activate FAA
        FAA -> ES: write audit record
        activate ES
        ES --> FAA: acknowledged
        deactivate ES
        FAA --> AS: committed
        deactivate FAA

        AS --> SI: 403 Forbidden
        SI --> user: access denied
    end
end

group Segregation of Duties Check
    AS -> AS: check SoD constraints
    note right of AS
        Verify no SoD violations:
        - creator cannot approve own work
        - author cannot waive own findings
        - conflicting role pairs enforced
    end note

    alt SoD Violation
        AS -> FAA: append SoDDenied event
        activate FAA
        FAA -> ES: write audit record
        activate ES
        ES --> FAA: acknowledged
        deactivate ES
        FAA --> AS: committed
        deactivate FAA

        AS --> SI: 403 Forbidden
        SI --> user: access denied
    end
end

== Authorized Path ==

AS -> AS: proceed with operation
note right of AS
    All authorization checks passed.
    Execute the requested operation.
end note

AS --> SI: operation result
deactivate AS

SI --> user: response
deactivate SI

note right of FAA
    All authorization decisions
    (allow and deny) are audited.
    Append-only, immutable log.
end note

footer SEQ-008 | Selma Project | Authorization Check

@enduml
